<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Admin | Security | {{siteName}}</title>
    {{>partials/head-deps.hbs}}
    {{>partials/head-styles.hbs}}
</head>
<body>
{{>partials/admin-shell.hbs}}
    <h1>Security</h1>
    {{#saved}}<div class="alert alert-success" role="alert"><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline" aria-hidden="true"></i> Security settings saved.</div>{{/saved}}

    <h2><i class="mdi mdi-shield-lock-outline" aria-hidden="true"></i> Content Security Policy</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary" style="max-width:52rem">The Content-Security-Policy header tells browsers which
        sources a page may load scripts, styles, fonts, images, etc. from  as a defense against cross-site
        scripting. WikiKT ships a baseline that keeps the app working with its default CDNs and other hosted files; you can
        add extra trusted sources per directive to enable sources the baseline doesn't allow
        (e.g. a self-hosted font server, another CDN, analytics, etc.). Changes add to (but do not remove from) the baseline to
        avoid changes below breaking core site functionality.</p>
    <p class="text-secondary" style="max-width:52rem">List sources, separated by new lines or spaces. A source may be a host
        (<code>https://cdn.example.com</code>), a wildcard host (<code>https://*.example.com</code>), or a scheme
        (<code>https:</code>, <code>data:</code>). Invalid entries will be pruned on save.</p>

    <form method="post" action="/a/security" class="edit-form" style="max-width:52rem">
        {{{csrfField}}}
        {{#cspDirectives}}
        <div class="mb-3">
            <label class="form-label" for="{{field}}"><code>{{name}}</code> <span class="text-secondary">— {{label}}</span></label>
            <textarea class="form-control" style="font-family:var(--bs-font-monospace);font-size:0.85rem" id="{{field}}" name="{{field}}" rows="2" spellcheck="false" placeholder="https://cdn.example.com" maxlength="2000">{{value}}</textarea>
            <p class="form-text mb-0">Baseline: <code>{{baseline}}</code></p>
        </div>
        {{/cspDirectives}}

        <div class="form-check mb-3">
            <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="cspReportOnly" id="cspReportOnly" value="1" {{#cspReportOnly}}checked{{/cspReportOnly}}>
            <label class="form-check-label" for="cspReportOnly">Report-only mode (log violations to browser console instead of blocking)</label>
            <p class="form-text">Sends <code>Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only</code> instead of enforcing. Use it to
                test a change safely: nothing will be blocked, but violations will be reported in the browser dev-tools console.
                Turn back off (recommended for production deployment) to enforce.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary"><i class="mdi mdi-content-save-outline" aria-hidden="true"></i> Save policy</button>
    </form>

    <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Fixed directives</h3>
    <p class="text-secondary" style="max-width:52rem">These directives are part of the baseline and cannot be removed; presented for information only:</p>
    <ul class="list-unstyled" style="font-family:var(--bs-font-monospace);font-size:0.85rem">
        {{#cspFixed}}<li><code>{{name}}</code> {{sources}}</li>{{/cspFixed}}
    </ul>

    <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Effective policy</h3>
    <p class="text-secondary">Preview of <code>{{cspEffectiveHeader}}</code> header as currently sent with every page on the site:</p>
    <div class="border rounded p-3 bg-body-tertiary" style="font-family:var(--bs-font-monospace);font-size:0.82rem;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word">{{cspEffectiveValue}}</div>
{{>partials/admin-shell-end.hbs}}
{{{bodyHtml}}}</body>
</html>
